{:edb/db-before-t 2834 :edb/db-after-t 2835 :edb/tx-data [[13194139536147 50 #inst "2026-10-09T16:57:35.583Z" 13194139536147 true] [17592186087807 1020 #edb/ref 17592186386079 13194139536147 true] [17592186088080 1100 "Which of the following first-order linear differential equations are homogeneous?\n\n- ${y}^{′}+2xy=0$\n- ${y}^{′}+2xy=4$\n- ${y}^{′}+2xy=-y$" 13194139536147 true] [17592186088080 1100 "Which of the following first-order linear differential equations are homogeneous?\n\n1. $y^{\\prime } + 2xy = 0$\n2. $y^{\\prime } + 2xy = 4$\n3. $y^{\\prime } + 2xy =-y$" 13194139536147 false] [17592186088080 1145 "A first-order linear differential equation is homogeneous if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+P(x)y=0.\n$$\n\nNow, let's consider each equation in turn.\n\n- First, we consider the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+2xy=0.\n$$\n\nThe right-hand side is already zero, so the equation directly matches the form ${y}^{′}+P(x)y=0.$ Therefore, this equation is homogeneous.\n\n- Next, we consider the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+2xy=4.\n$$\n\nThe presence of the constant term $4$ means the right-hand side is not zero, and so it cannot be rewritten in homogeneous form. Thus, this equation is *not* homogeneous.\n\n- Finally, we consider the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+2xy=-y.\n$$\n\nWe move the term involving $y$ to the left side so that all $y$-terms are together:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}+2xy & =-y \\\\ {y}^{′}+2xy+y & =0 \\\\ {y}^{′}+(2x+1)y & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis matches the homogeneous form ${y}^{′}+P(x)y=0.$  Therefore, this equation *is* homogeneous.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" 13194139536147 true] [17592186088080 1145 "Collect all terms involving $y$ on the left. Equation I already has zero forcing and is homogeneous. Equation II has forcing $4$, so it is inhomogeneous. Equation III becomes $y^{\\prime}+(2x+1)y=0$, so it is homogeneous. Therefore the answer is I and III only." 13194139536147 false] [17592186386079 1017 #edb/ref 17592186386080 13194139536147 true] [17592186386079 1089 "q-331743" 13194139536147 true] [17592186386079 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536147 true] [17592186386079 1100 "Which of the following first-order linear differential equations are inhomogeneous?\n\n- ${y}^{′}+{x}^{2}y=-2$\n- ${y}^{′}+{x}^{2}y=y$\n- ${y}^{′}+{x}^{2}y=0$" 13194139536147 true] [17592186386079 1113 #uuid "a1b74dfd-adf9-57b0-bcdb-a5d1bb8aab44" 13194139536147 true] [17592186386079 1145 "A first-order linear differential equation is homogeneous if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+P(x)y=0.\n$$\n\nA first-order linear differential equation is inhomogeneous if it is not homogeneous, i.e., if it can be written as\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwhere $Q$ is not identical to zero.\n\nTo determine which equations are inhomogeneous, we examine each one in turn.\n\n- First, we consider the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+{x}^{2}y=-2.\n$$\n\nNotice that this is written in the form ${y}^{′}+P(x)y=Q(x)$ where $Q(x)=-2$ is not identically zero. Therefore, this equation is inhomogeneous.\n\n- Next, we consider the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+{x}^{2}y=y.\n$$\n\nWe collect the $y$-terms on the left side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}+{x}^{2}y & =y \\\\ {y}^{′}+{x}^{2}y-y & =0 \\\\ {y}^{′}+({x}^{2}-1)y & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis matches the homogeneous form ${y}^{′}+P(x)y=0.$  Therefore, this equation *is* homogeneous.\n\n- Finally, we consider the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+{x}^{2}y=0.\n$$\n\nThe right-hand side is already zero, so the equation directly matches the form ${y}^{′}+P(x)y=0.$ Therefore, this equation is homogeneous.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" 13194139536147 true] [17592186386080 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386081 13194139536147 true] [17592186386080 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386082 13194139536147 true] [17592186386080 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386083 13194139536147 true] [17592186386080 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386084 13194139536147 true] [17592186386080 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386085 13194139536147 true] [17592186386080 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536147 true] [17592186386080 1041 "selection" 13194139536147 true] [17592186386080 1104 #edb/ref 17592186386082 13194139536147 true] [17592186386080 1110 #uuid "8cc37fe2-954d-5e08-a1ba-f082d6c3af58" 13194139536147 true] [17592186386081 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139536147 true] [17592186386081 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536147 true] [17592186386081 1111 #uuid "e66b7bb7-de58-5b63-b773-99eeb9f86408" 13194139536147 true] [17592186386082 1034 "I only" 13194139536147 true] [17592186386082 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536147 true] [17592186386082 1111 #uuid "db9cfafe-095c-5983-93ef-120b9a0ffabc" 13194139536147 true] [17592186386083 1034 "III only" 13194139536147 true] [17592186386083 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536147 true] [17592186386083 1111 #uuid "587cefac-0d76-58d9-bda7-f54c1dcec7e3" 13194139536147 true] [17592186386084 1034 "I and II only" 13194139536147 true] [17592186386084 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536147 true] [17592186386084 1111 #uuid "ab81c4ed-be1e-5088-ab92-e9a3369ce608" 13194139536147 true] [17592186386085 1034 "II only" 13194139536147 true] [17592186386085 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536147 true] [17592186386085 1111 #uuid "418bf5a7-8e73-5736-8336-eac2ebb290b7" 13194139536147 true]] :edb/tempids {"q-331743" 17592186386079 "q-331743/selection" 17592186386080 "q-331743/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" 17592186386081 "q-331743/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" 17592186386082 "q-331743/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" 17592186386083 "q-331743/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" 17592186386084 "q-331743/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" 17592186386085} :edb/committed false :edb/speculative true}
